<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Ferry: Rust crate licences</title>
<style>
  body { font: 14px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 60rem; padding: 0 1rem; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1rem; overflow-x: auto; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { background: #1e1e1e; color: #ddd; } pre { background: #2a2a2a; } a { color: #8ab4f8; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Rust crates linked into Ferry</h1>
<p>Ferry is GPL-3.0-or-later. It includes the open-source Rust crates below. Crates under the Mozilla Public License 2.0
are used unmodified; their source is on crates.io at the version in Ferry's Cargo.lock. See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.</p>

<h2>Licences</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
  <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>

{{#each licenses}}
<h2 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h2>
<h3>Used by</h3>
<ul>
{{#each used_by}}
  <li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}{{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
